# PERF-LOSSY-LOW env-gate — 2026-06-10 (/goal hunt, lossy e3/e4/e5 landscape)
#
# The profile that found it (radix2 binary, -d 1.0 1T, terminal+clic097):
#   e3/e4: std::env getenv 14.3-17.2% + env-RwLock read_contended
#   5.9-12.2% + CStr::from_bytes_with_nul 5.5-7.6% — 25-35% of CPU in
#   std::env::var machinery. Cause: the W44-era diagnostic dump hooks
#   probe their env vars PER BLOCK on the bitstream/AC paths.
#
# Fix: once-per-process PRESENCE gate (OnceLock<bool>) on all five
# per-call dump-hook reads — JXL_W44_76_PER_BLOCK_DUMP,
# JXL_W44_201_COEFFS_DUMP, JXL_W44_182_DUMP_CFL,
# JXL_W44_AUDIT_8_P4_DUMP, JXL_DUMP_POS. Absent at first probe =>
# permanently disabled, zero further env reads; present => per-call
# re-reads keep the documented repoint-between-images behaviour.
# SEMANTICS NOTE: hooks must now be set before the process's first
# encode (all known drivers already do).
#
# Gates: lossy bytes identical 9/9 (terminal/clic097/mobile x e3/e4/e5,
# -d 1.0); hash-locks 36/36 x2; libjxl byte-locks 5/5; lib 1488; it 58.
#
# Walls (8 iters/side interleaved, loadavg ~4.4):
#   e3: terminal -6.40%  clic097 -6.03%  mobile -6.79%
#   e4: terminal -8.40%  clic097 -7.50%  mobile -7.71%
#   e5: terminal -3.03%  clic097 -1.42%  mobile -0.36%
# Host: lilith (7950X, WSL2).
#
# ── ADDENDUM: sixth hook (w44_181_dump::dump_dc, JXL_W44_181_DUMP_DC) ──────
# The post-fix profile showed residual getenv 6.7% + RwLock 5.3% at e3;
# dwarf callgraph attributed it to w44_181_dump::dump_dc probing per
# block from transform_blocks_into (missed by the first sweep — sixth
# module). Same once-presence gate applied. Walls: ~NEUTRAL
# (-0.65..+0.29% on 0.14-0.21s cells) — the env-RwLock contention had
# already collapsed once the other five hooks stopped hammering, leaving
# uncontended getenv below the noise floor. Shipped as byte-identical
# consistency hygiene (all six dump modules now share the gate pattern);
# bytes identical 6/6, env-fallback/dispatch override tests 20/20.
#
# ── ADDENDUM 2: proxy-skip at e<5 && d<2 ───────────────────────────────────
# ZenanalyzeProxies::compute_srgb_u8 (the W44 content-classifier full-res
# RGB sweep) was 24% of e3 d=1 CPU yet every consumer is banded to
# effort>=5 (W44-164/2c classifier) or distance>=2.0 (W44-91/96/98/124
# discriminators) — computed-and-discarded at e3/e4 d<2. Skip predicate
# `effort >= 5 || distance >= 2.0` at the api.rs assignment site.
# Bytes identical 12/12 across e{3,4,5} x d{1.0,3.0} (both sides of
# every band edge); hash-locks x2 + libjxl byte-locks 5/5. The two
# co-scheduled it-failures during gating were the DOCUMENTED env-
# parallel flake (Known Bugs 2026-06-10) — both pass in isolation.
# Walls (8 iters/side, load 2.6, -d 1.0):
#   e3: terminal -20.44%  clic097 -19.82%  mobile -18.06%
#   e4: terminal -17.41%  clic097 -19.84%  mobile -18.87%
# Combined with the env-gates: lossy e3/e4 day delta ~ -25%.
# Remaining at e5+/d>=2: compute_srgb_u8 is REAL consumer cost (the
# classifier feeds active gates) — pinned as legitimate work; its f64
# accumulation order is byte-relevant, so SIMD reassociation is not
# byte-safe without re-locking.
#
# ── ADDENDUM 3: __env_var_diagnostics feature (user-proposed) ───────────────
# All DIAGNOSTIC dump env hooks now compile out entirely by default:
# the 4 dump modules (w44_76 block+coeffs, w44_181 DC, w44_182 CfL,
# w44_audit_8_p4 DC), JXL_DUMP_POS, the ac_strategy cost-input/AFV
# dumps, coeff_order W44-200/201 dumps, epf SA_C dump, cfl Newton dump,
# and __JXL_ENC_PHASE_TIMING. Opt back in with
# `--features __env_var_diagnostics` (CLI passthrough exists); the 15
# dump-driver examples carry required-features so they fail LOUD
# without it. Behaviour-override hooks (W44 gate fallbacks, dispatch
# disables, buttloop scales) intentionally stay runtime — the override
# test contract + A/B harnesses depend on them in production builds.
# Proofs: hook-name strings count 0 in the default release binary;
# hash-locks 36/36 in default AND parallel-tree-learning AND feature-on
# configs (compiled-feature byte-invariance); libjxl byte-locks 5/5;
# lib 1488 both combos; bytes identical 4/4 (lossless e7 + lossy e3,
# terminal + clic097) vs the pre-feature binary; feature-on smoke dump
# verified writing. Supersedes the runtime once-presence gates as the
# default-path mechanism (the gates remain inside the feature for the
# hook-set-but-unused case).
